{"title":"2001 IMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/06547710ff1b79d2baf182222f5aebf64ccbfcfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K &gt; L &gt; M &gt; N$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"138\" height=\"13\" /> are positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/3/98352545985272c9be427242deb73b67a4f2af2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KM + LN = (K + L - M + N)(-K + L + M + N)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"416\" height=\"18\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d191db5611768a179ef3b510ed2343b71628711.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL + MN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" /> is not prime.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/5/3b50bebaa3acf87b94ad6005f9a69f0c09bda8dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(KL+MN)-(KM+LN)=(K-N)(L-M)&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"420\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/b/f7ba1ec5f5a34e4ef6542f42dbd5678ea876df68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K&gt;N$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"57\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/a/c8add67cd6dbbfe29bf70a4df4128b174148f6be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L&gt;M$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/b/54b6dc8a7ee18547892acdacb5c533210d23e253.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL+MN&gt;KM+LN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"199\" height=\"14\" />.  \n</p><p>Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/1/92169ee27e6bdeb8377a205ce16df00185ae31b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(KM+LN)-(KN+LM)=(K-L)(M-N)&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"420\" height=\"18\" /> since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/9/44990469aa1669c0ce1c87a486e9a2c2e5d138af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K&gt;L$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"53\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/7568409324f5fac95cb73c74f7324cc39b85065c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M&gt;N$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/c/49c4bfe36a63afa1a06d951f095006207259824b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KM+LN&gt;KN+LM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"199\" height=\"14\" />.  \n</p><p>Putting the two together, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/3/b73cbb5d01685618dbc9cafdd1d62190452bd70d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[KL+MN&gt;KM+LN&gt;KN+LM\\]\" width=\"310\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Now, we have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/9/7a99ee04b887a106c1b9d78ac77d5548e6f58938.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(K+L-M+N)(-K+L+M+N)=KM+LN\\]\" width=\"416\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/f/21f12dfe67e32efe846a3055b2c73bf2099cf3cd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[-K^2+KM+L^2+LN+KM-M^2+LN+N^2=KM+LN\\]\" width=\"478\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/0190a09c7d4c8942494ab50f7abaa29f83390e26.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[L^2+LN+N^2=K^2-KM+M^2\\]\" width=\"272\" height=\"16\" />\nSo, we have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/1/8c15b88e1a33d5b91c72a42331683e49293a5d0c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(KM+LN)(L^2+LN+N^2)=KM(L^2+LN+N^2)+LN(L^2+LN+N^2)\\]\" width=\"540\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/6/7666a4367eecf0ea931718ca8f8978382e6e62df.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=KM(L^2+LN+N^2)+LN(K^2-KM+M^2)\\]\" width=\"381\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/8/a8822c39c72061d1bc7d5b1af2373d172a618eff.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=KML^2+KMN^2+K^2LN+LM^2N\\]\" width=\"310\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/8/338472c3dca1f367f7d522d61b15fe49fed07dda.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=(KL+MN)(KN+LM)\\]\" width=\"220\" height=\"18\" />\nThus, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/d/67d2cb1de4dd0212d569c188b7632220ac4bbe9f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(KM+LN) \\mid (KL+MN)(KN+LM).\\]\" width=\"322\" height=\"18\" />  \nNow, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/b/54b6dc8a7ee18547892acdacb5c533210d23e253.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL+MN&gt;KM+LN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"199\" height=\"14\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/7/d37b1864d9e3969165c09dbe7ac606675a6ef1f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL+MN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" /> is prime, then there are no common factors between the two.  So, in order to have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/0879e3460c5c35fa23b99a9102d3327de7f2cc6e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(KM+LN)\\mid (KL+MN)(KN+LM),\\]\" width=\"322\" height=\"18\" /> we would have to have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/0/52003afc5d5c0082dbcfb6f39a1d3007d8fb758c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(KM+LN) \\mid (KN+LM).\\]\" width=\"220\" height=\"18\" /> This is impossible as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/c/49c4bfe36a63afa1a06d951f095006207259824b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KM+LN&gt;KN+LM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"199\" height=\"14\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/7/d37b1864d9e3969165c09dbe7ac606675a6ef1f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$KL+MN$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" /> must be composite.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO\" title=\"2001 IMO\">2001 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2001 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2001 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Problem</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017093817\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.020 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.033 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 162/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 865/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 50/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4733/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.795      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.795      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7339:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017093817 and revision id 204488. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}